    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d487">

                <pb facs="0685" n="671" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg671"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11–844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-08T18:00:00+07:00">November 8, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 8—1:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1800. 1. We are now informed by a member that PPC investigation party expects to
                    leave next week for Yenan. (Retel 1781, November 4, 5 p.m.) Members of party are
                    said to feel that hopes of Kmt–CCP<anchor n="55a" xml:id="d487-f1"/>
                    <pb facs="0686" n="672" xml:id="pg672"/> settlement are small but are
                    nevertheless worth exploring. We are of opinion that mission is unlikely to
                    result in any concrete accomplishment.</p>
                <p>2. Local office of CCP newspaper was reportedly raided by local authorities [on]
                    4th and quantity of Communist literature seized.</p>
                <p>3. According to local representative of independent guerilla group operating in
                    Shantung (Redes 072 [<hi rendition="#italic">3072</hi>], October 18<anchor
                        n="56" xml:id="d487-f2"/>), Communist Eighth Route and New Fourth Armies
                    have recently launched military attacks on independent guerilla areas in
                    Shantung and North Kiangsu in endeavor to liquidate latter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
